      "title": "BlackBerry Jumps 13.3% in a Week as QNX and Earnings Momentum Build",
      "summary": "BlackBerry (BB) surged 13.3% in a week following stronger-than-expected earnings, with QNX revenues jumping 27.3% to a record $80.3 million and adjusted EBITDA rising 41.5%. The company raised fiscal 2027 guidance across revenue, EBITDA, and operating cash flow. However, the stock trades at 8.0X EV/Sales versus its 5-year median of 3.8X, creating a higher execution bar. Secure Communications showed weakness with declining net retention at 91%, and the company faces contract-timing risks. BB holds a Zacks Rank #3 (Hold) rating with strong Growth and Momentum scores but weak Value score.",
